# Shared bastion / containerlab access variables
#
# EXAMPLE VALUES ARE FOR hlxcl7 — do not copy blindly. Replace for your lab:
#   KUBECONFIG / OPENPE_KUBECONFIG             — cluster under test
#   OPENPE_UNDERLAY_IFACE                      — real worker secondary NIC (not toswitch*)
#   OPENPE_BASTION_NODE_IP_BASE                — underlay host octet (.103/.104 on hlxcl7)
#   OPENPE_E2E_NAMESPACE                       — openperouter-system vs openshift-openperouter
#   CLAB_BASTION_LAB_IFACE_* / VLAN notes      — guest NICs and HV VLAN map
#   OPENPE_E2E_NODE_SELECTOR                   — workers / workercnf MCP label
#   CLAB_BASTION_HOST/SSH/WORKDIR              — unused when CLAB_EXECUTOR=local (optional)
#
# Cluster 7 dual-leaf lab map (HV tags VLANs; guest NICs are untagged):
#   VLAN 101 → eth1 → toswitch1 → leafkind1
#   VLAN 177 → eth2 → toswitch2 → leafkind2
#   eth0     = mgmt / SSH / default route only
#   VLAN 178 = spare (MetalLB / future)
#
#   set -a && source openshift/e2e/bastion.env.example && set +a
#   ./openshift/e2e/setup-bastion-bridges.sh
#
# Do NOT put a default gateway on lab ifaces (breaks SSH/mgmt on eth0).
# setup-bastion-bridges.sh pins NM: eth0 = mgmt; eth1/eth2 = ipv4/ipv6 disabled + never-default.

CLAB_EXECUTOR=local
CLAB_BASTION_MGMT_IFACE=eth0

# Shared/future remote-bastion vars (e.g. MetalLB laptop→bastion). Not used by the
# current OpenPE path when CLAB_EXECUTOR=local (scripts run on the bastion itself).
# CLAB_BASTION_HOST=registry.hlxcl7.lab.eng.tlv2.redhat.com
# CLAB_BASTION_USER=telcov10n
# CLAB_BASTION_SSH=telcov10n@registry.hlxcl7.lab.eng.tlv2.redhat.com
# CLAB_BASTION_WORKDIR=/home/telcov10n/openperouter

CLAB_RUNTIME=podman

# Dual lab NICs → OpenPE toswitch bridges
CLAB_BASTION_LAB_IFACE_TOSWITCH1=eth1
CLAB_BASTION_LAB_IFACE_TOSWITCH2=eth2
CLAB_BASTION_ATTACH_LAB_IFACE=true

# Back-compat alias (toswitch1 leg)
CLAB_BASTION_LAB_IFACE=eth1

OPENPE_E2E_PROVIDER=bastion
OPENPE_CLAB_RUNTIME=${CLAB_RUNTIME}
OPENPE_BASTION_LAB_IFACE=${CLAB_BASTION_LAB_IFACE}
OPENPE_BASTION_ATTACH_LAB_IFACE=${CLAB_BASTION_ATTACH_LAB_IFACE}
# Skip leafSRV6/hostSRV6_* setups (bastion script default is already true).
# SRv6 sysctls hang this bastion under podman — set false only to opt in.
OPENPE_BASTION_SKIP_SRV6_SETUP=true
# Ginkgo container CLI: must see rootful clab (setup uses sudo podman).
# run_tests.sh defaults to openshift/e2e/podman-root.sh when provider=bastion.
# CONTAINER_RUNTIME=openshift/e2e/podman-root.sh

# Cluster kubeconfig (required). hlxcl7 path — replace for your lab.
# Scripts (e2e-bastion.sh / run_tests.sh / deploy-bastion.sh) read KUBECONFIG.
# make e2e-bastion requires OPENPE_KUBECONFIG and exports it as KUBECONFIG
# (Makefile refuses the KIND default kubeconfig). Either:
#   export OPENPE_KUBECONFIG=/path/to/ocp/kubeconfig && make e2e-bastion
# or uncomment and source this file, then run scripts / make with OPENPE_KUBECONFIG set:
# KUBECONFIG=/home/telcov10n/project/generated/hlxcl7/auth/kubeconfig
# OPENPE_KUBECONFIG=${KUBECONFIG}

# Only include underlay-capable nodes in nodelink.json (masters excluded).
# CNF MCP workercnf → often: node-role.kubernetes.io/workercnf
# ECO: ECO_CNF_CORE_NET_CNF_MCP_LABEL=workercnf
OPENPE_E2E_NODE_SELECTOR=node-role.kubernetes.io/worker
# Keep .103/.104 if those IPs are already on workers:
# OPENPE_BASTION_NODE_IP_BASE=103

# run_tests.sh focus/skip (regex). Default expands beyond Single Session Baseline.
# OPENPE_E2E_FOCUS='Single.Session.Baseline|Node.Router.Status|Router.BGP.sessions|North/south.traffic.after.FRR'
# OPENPE_E2E_NAMESPACE=openperouter-system

# CNO FRR (frr-k8s) — defaults match deploy-bastion / teardown_frrk8s (both false):
# telco QE treats FRR as shared lab infra; e2e only waits for existing pods.
OPENPE_E2E_DEPLOY_FRRK8S=false
OPENPE_E2E_TEARDOWN_FRRK8S=false
# FRRK8S_NAMESPACE=openshift-frr-k8s   # shared by deploy/teardown/run_tests
#
# --- Greenfield / non-telco (CNO FRR NOT already enabled) ---
# If openshift-frr-k8s is missing, deploy-bastion fails with "set …=true or enable
# CNO FRR first". Uncomment BOTH so this job enables FRR and restores CNO on EXIT:
#   OPENPE_E2E_DEPLOY_FRRK8S=true
#   OPENPE_E2E_TEARDOWN_FRRK8S=true   # marker → restore providersBefore
# Do not set deploy=true with teardown=false on a shared cluster (leaves FRR on).
# OPENPE_E2E_TEARDOWN_FRRK8S=force    # always drop FRR from current providers

# Worker underlay IPs: applied before Ginkgo, removed on EXIT (configure/teardown-bastion-worker-net).
# Bastion is single-homed by default (one worker NIC → leafkind1). That matches
# DualLeafEnabled / setup-clab nodelink (no leaf2 unless IFACE2 is set).
# configure applies IPv4 only (nodelink may still list ipv6* for future / KIND parity).
# run_tests.sh exports these for Ginkgo (make e2etests); if unset, hydrates from
# .e2e-bastion-state/worker-net.json written by configure.
OPENPE_E2E_TEARDOWN_WORKER_NET=true
# hlxcl7 MLX NIC + .103/.104 — replace iface/base for your lab
OPENPE_UNDERLAY_IFACE=ens8f0np0
OPENPE_BASTION_NODE_IP_BASE=103
# Dual-leaf opt-in (second worker NIC → leafkind2); also enables DualLeafEnabled in Go tests:
# OPENPE_UNDERLAY_IFACE2=ens8f1np1

# Skip *all* EXIT cleanup (worker-net + clab + frrk8s). Not fabric-only.
# Prefer OPENPE_E2E_TEARDOWN_WORKER_NET / OPENPE_E2E_TEARDOWN_FRRK8S for selective skips.
# OPENPE_E2E_SKIP_TEARDOWN=true
